{"name":"Tassel Taupe","hex":"#9f9291","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tassel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ball-shaped bunch of plaited or otherwise entangled threads from which at one end protrudes a cord on which the ball is hung, and which may have loose, dangling threads at the other end (often used as decoration along the bottom of garments, curtains or other hangings).","The panicle on a male plant of maize, which consists of loose threads with anthers on them."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To adorn with tassels.","To put forth a tassel or flower."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tassel"},{"term":"taupe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark brownish-grey colour, the colour of moleskin."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark brownish-grey colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taupe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tassel","blocks":[{"text":"A tassel is a finishing feature in fabric and clothing decoration. It is a universal ornament that is seen in varying versions in many cultures around the globe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tassel2.svg/330px-Tassel2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tassel","wikidata":"Q1194132"},{"title":"Taupe","blocks":[{"text":"Taupe is a dark gray-brown color. The word derives from the French noun taupe meaning \"mole\". The name originally referred only to the average color of the French mole, but beginning in the 1940s, its usage expanded to encompass a wider range of shades."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taupe","wikidata":"Q2307593"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Orna118-Quasten.png/500px-Orna118-Quasten.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Orna118-Q